# ─── AI Provider Configuration ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Two providers are supported. Switch by changing the values below.
# No code changes are needed — only this file differs between environments.
#
# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ OPTION 1 — Ollama (local, free, recommended for development)            │
# │                                                                         │
# │  LLM_PROVIDER=ollama                                                    │
# │  EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=ollama                                              │
# │  GEMINI_API_KEY=          (leave blank)                                 │
# │                                                                         │
# │  Prerequisites (one-time setup):                                        │
# │    ollama pull all-minilm     ← embeddings (Check FAQ / Ask Question)  │
# │    ollama pull gemma3:4b      ← LLM (Yaksha chatbot)                   │
# │                                                                         │
# │  Pros: completely free, works offline, no rate limits.                  │
# │  Cons: requires Ollama running locally; not suitable for production     │
# │        servers (high RAM usage, no horizontal scaling).                 │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ OPTION 2 — Google Gemini API (recommended for production)               │
# │                                                                         │
# │  LLM_PROVIDER=gemini                                                    │
# │  EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=gemini                                              │
# │  GEMINI_API_KEY=your_key_here                                           │
# │                                                                         │
# │  Get a free API key at: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey             │
# │                                                                         │
# │  Free-tier rate limits (as of 2026):                                    │
# │    text-embedding-004  (Check FAQ / Ask Question)                       │
# │      → 1,500 requests/minute — more than sufficient for an internship   │
# │        portal with hundreds of simultaneous students.                   │
# │    gemini-2.0-flash  (Yaksha chatbot replies)                           │
# │      → 1,500 requests/day, 15 requests/minute on the free tier.        │
# │        For a cohort of 300 students asking ~5 questions each = 1,500   │
# │        total — fits exactly within the free daily quota.                │
# │        Upgrade to the paid tier (~$0.10 per 1M tokens) if you exceed   │
# │        this, which only happens with very active cohorts.               │
# │                                                                         │
# │  Pros: no server RAM cost, scales to thousands of users, high accuracy. │
# │  Cons: requires internet; usage above free tier incurs small cost.      │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
# See apps/server/AI_SETUP.md for full documentation, alternative providers,
# and the roadmap for Option D (LLM synthesis in the Ask Question flow).
#
# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ OPTION 3 — Gemini embeddings + Groq LLM (best free-tier combination)   │
# │                                                                         │
# │  EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=gemini   ← Check FAQ / Check Community Questions   │
# │  LLM_PROVIDER=groq           ← Yaksha chatbot replies                  │
# │  GEMINI_API_KEY=your_key     ← from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey │
# │  GROQ_API_KEY=your_key       ← from https://console.groq.com           │
# │                                                                         │
# │  Why this combination is best for production:                           │
# │    Gemini text-embedding-004 → 1,500 embedding req/min (free)          │
# │    Groq llama-3.3-70b        → 14,400 chat req/day (free)              │
# │      (10× the daily quota of Gemini's chat model)                      │
# │    Groq is also significantly faster — ~300ms vs ~2s for Gemini chat.  │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
# See apps/server/AI_SETUP.md for full documentation and the Option D roadmap.
#
# ── Active configuration ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Gemini — embeddings (Check FAQ + Check Community Questions):
EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=gemini
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Chatbot LLM (Yaksha) — using Ollama locally (free, no API cost):
LLM_PROVIDER=ollama

# Groq key stored here for future use if you decide to switch the chatbot to Groq.
# To activate: change LLM_PROVIDER=groq above.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Ollama — kept as local fallback (embeddings + LLM if API keys are removed):
# LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
# EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=ollama
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
OLLAMA_MODEL=gemma3:4b
